      <metadata>
        <description><![CDATA[{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
{\*\listtable{\list\listtemplateid1{\listlevel\levelnfc23\levelnfcn23\leveljc0\leveljcn0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1\levelindent0{\leveltext\'01\u8226 ?;}{\levelnumbers;}\fi-360\li360\lin360 }{\listname ;}\listid1}
}
{\*\listoverridetable{\listoverride\listid1\listoverridecount0\ls1}}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 List of Instruments and Effects\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Lists all REAPER plugins used in an active project, grouping them into categories. The motivation comes from the KVR One Synth Challenge competition, which requires providing technical details of the production.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Results appear in the window immediately, with buttons to copy them to the clipboard in several formats:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} {\b plain text} -- the text shown in the preview window\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} {\b markdown} -- results formatted into tables\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} {\b BB plain} -- some BBCode formatting, such as bold\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} {\b BB code} -- wrapped in {\f1 \fs24 [CODE]} tags to force a fixed-width font\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every press of a Copy button regenerates the report, refreshing what is displayed. Normally the window shows plain text whichever export format is selected; tick {\f1 \fs24 debug} to make it show exactly what goes to the clipboard.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires {\b Lokasenna's GUI library v2 for Lua}, available on ReaPack. After installing it, run {\i Set Lokasenna_GUI v2 library path.lua} once from the Action List.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Written and tested in REAPER 7.x; it may work in earlier versions. GPL v3.\par}
}
]]></description>
